# Blazor conventions

Use the same **tooling habits** as the rest of the solution (`#region #`, consistent file layout) — but **do not copy C# data-layer or AI-layer grouping or region names into Blazor**. They answer different questions.

## C# data layer vs Blazor — two perspectives

| | **C# (Features, Persistence, DTOs)** | **Blazor (`@code`)** |
|---|--------------------------------------|----------------------|
| **Organized by** | Entity, operation, technical step | User action, UI concern, screen behavior |
| **Region names** | Entity/type: `# ChatThread`, `# User` | Activity: `# List/Select ChatThreads`, `# Rename ChatThread` |
| **Shared state** | Constructor params (`_repo`, `_ctx`) | Preamble at top of `@code` (`_threads`) |
| **Shared logic** | Private methods in same class / layer | `# Helpers` at bottom of `@code` |
| **Lifecycle** | N/A | Preamble only — never inside a feature region |
| **Inner method blocks** | `# Validate`, `# Execute`, `# Handle Result` | Same — still mirror `Features` inside a handler |

**C# asks:** “Which entity or API operation is this?”  
**Blazor asks:** “What is the user doing on this component?”

Region names in `.razor` files can be shorter and plainer than C# when it helps readability. Prefer clarity over matching `Features` method names exactly.

## File layout (top to bottom)

1. **Directives** (see order below) — blank line after the last directive
2. **`<PageTitle>`** — routable pages only
3. **Markup**
4. **`@code { }`** — or a sibling `ComponentName.razor.cs` partial when `@code` is large

### Directive order

Use only what the file needs, in this order:

1. `@page`
2. `@layout`
3. `@rendermode`
4. `@inherits` — `BaseComponent` for app components; `LayoutComponentBase` for layouts
5. `@implements`
6. `@attribute`
7. `@using` — only namespaces **not** in `_Imports.razor`; System first, then Microsoft, then `WebApp.*` (alphabetical within each group)
8. `@inject` — avoid when inheriting `BaseComponent` (injections live on the base class)

**Do not** repeat `@using` already declared in `Components/_Imports.razor`.

### Global usings (`_Imports.razor`)

Framework and app-wide namespaces belong here, not on every page.

## Inheritance

| Component kind | Inherits |
|----------------|----------|
| Pages, layout parts with logic (Sidebar, Navbar if needed) | `BaseComponent` |
| `MainLayout`, other layout roots | `LayoutComponentBase` |
| `App.razor`, `Routes.razor`, static markup-only | No base (or `BaseComponent` only when injections are needed) |

Shared members on `BaseComponent`:

- `Features`, `NavigationManager`, `JsRuntime` — injected properties use **PascalCase** (Blazor convention)
- `NotifyLayoutRefresh` — cascading parameter (PascalCase)
- `RefreshLayoutAsync()`

`BaseComponent` uses `#region # Init` for injections and cascading parameters (`.cs` base class only).

## `@code` block layout

Three layers, in this order:

### 1. Preamble (no region)

Put at the **top** of `@code`, **outside** any `#region`:

- **Shared state** used across multiple areas (e.g. `_threads`, `_messages`, `[Parameter]` properties)
- **All lifecycle overrides** (`OnInitializedAsync`, `OnParametersSetAsync`, `OnAfterRenderAsync`, `DisposeAsync`, etc.)

Never put lifecycle or shared fields inside a feature region.

Feature-specific fields that only one area uses may live inside that area’s region (e.g. rename fields under `# Rename ChatThread`).

Blank line, then regions.

### 2. Feature regions (middle)

Use `#region # Name` with `#` prefix (same marker as C#).

- Name regions by **what the user does** or **similar functionality grouped together** — not one region per API method.
- Combine related actions in one region when they stay focused (use `/` if helpful): e.g. `# List/Select ChatThreads`, `# Create/Delete ChatThread`, `# Rename ChatThread`.
- Regions are mostly **methods**; only include fields when they belong exclusively to that feature.
- Do **not** put shared or reusable logic here — move it to Helpers.

Order regions in a sensible user-flow order (load/list → mutate → edit → …).

### 3. `#region # Helpers` (last)

Always last. Dump anything **shared or cross-cutting**:

- Static parsers, formatters, validators
- Navigation/orchestration called from multiple regions
- JS interop (shell, scroll, keyboard)
- Thin wrappers that only exist to keep feature regions clean

If a method is used by more than one feature region, it belongs in Helpers.

## Method body pattern (inside feature methods)

For non-trivial calls to `Features`, mirror `Features.cs` with inner regions:

```csharp
#region # Validate
// guard clauses, early return
#endregion

#region # Execute
// call Features.*Async
#endregion

#region # Handle Result
// check HasError / Payload, update state
#endregion
```

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Injected services (base) | PascalCase (Blazor) | `Features`, `NavigationManager`, `JsRuntime` |
| Private component state | `_camelCase` | `_threads`, `_draft` |
| View models | `*ViewModel` | `SettingsViewModel` |
| Parameters / cascade | PascalCase | `ThreadId`, `NotifyLayoutRefresh` |
| Event handlers | `OnXxx` / `*Async` | `SendAsync`, `OnRenameBlurAsync` |
| Feature `#region` names | Short, UI-oriented; group related actions | `# List`, `# Create/Delete`, `# Rename` (or longer if clearer) |
| Inner method `#region` names | Match data layer | `# Validate`, `# Execute`, `# Handle Result` |
| CSS classes | kebab-case | `chat-shell`, `thread-list` |

**Note:** Underscore prefix (`_repo`, `_ctx`) is for the **data layer** (constructor-injected services), not for Blazor `[Inject]` properties.

## File location

Keep all UI under `Components/`:

- `Components/Pages/` — all routable pages
- `Components/Pages/{Area}/` — when routes share a URL prefix (e.g. `/auth/login` → `Pages/Auth/Login.razor`); `@page` keeps the full path
- `Components/Layout/` — layout roots only (`MainLayout`, `EmptyLayout`) and layout-scoped CSS
- `Components/Shared/` — non-routable components (auth helpers, shell chrome, reconnect modal, etc.)
- `Components/BaseComponent.cs` — shared base for interactive components (folder root, not `Shared/`)
- Optional: `Component.razor` + `Component.razor.cs` partial in the same folder

**Pages subfolders:** Use a subfolder when multiple pages share a route segment (`auth/login` → `Pages/Auth/`). Top-level `Pages/` is fine for single-segment routes (`/settings`, `/chat/...`, `/Error`).

**Page-local components:** When a page has multiple small, non-routable pieces used only on that page, use `Pages/{PageName}/{PageName}.razor` plus `Pages/{PageName}/Shared/` for widgets. Add `Pages/{PageName}/_Imports.razor` with `@using WebApp.Components.Pages.{PageName}.Shared`. Do not put page-local widgets in app-wide `Components/Shared/`.

**When to extract (page `Shared/`):** A distinct UI block with its own markup (or repeated structure), not tied to parent `@ref`/JS interop. **Do not extract:** static nav/aside with no logic; composer/input wired to parent refs; single small form sections; entire pages with one cohesive layout (Settings). **Auth:** route-prefix folder only (`Pages/Auth/Login.razor`) — no page `Shared/` until a second auth page needs shared fragments.

## Markup

- One blank line between major sections (header, list, footer)
- `aria-*` on interactive controls
- Prefer `NavLink` for in-app navigation

## Reference: Sidebar `@code` shape

```razor
@code {
    private List<GetChatThreadResponse> _threads = [];

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() { ... }
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender) { ... }

    #region # List
    // load + select
    #endregion

    #region # Create/Delete
    // new + remove (both mutate _threads and navigate)
    #endregion

    #region # Rename
    // rename-only fields + handlers
    #endregion

    #region # Helpers
    // IsThreadActive, NavigateToChatThreadAsync, JS shell, etc.
    #endregion
}
```

### Simplifying region names (optional)

Start long if needed; shorten when the file is familiar:

| Verbose (fine) | Shorter |
|----------------|---------|
| `# List/Select ChatThreads` | `# List` |
| `# Create/Delete ChatThread` | `# Create/Delete` |
| `# Rename ChatThread` | `# Rename` |
| `# Load/Show ChatMessages` + `# Send` | `# Messages` (load and send together) |
| `# Resolve ChatThread` | `# Thread` |

Do not split load and send into separate regions when both belong to the same UI surface (message list + composer).

## Reference: Chat `@code` shape

```razor
@code {
    [Parameter] public Guid? ThreadId { get; set; }
    // shared state, lifecycle, DisposeAsync

    #region # Thread
    // ResolveActiveThreadIdAsync — which conversation is open
    #endregion

    #region # Messages
    // SendFromJsAsync, LoadMessagesAsync, SendAsync
    // (inner # Execute / # Handle Result inside SendAsync as needed)
    #endregion

    #region # Helpers
    // ScrollToEndAsync, IsUser, AssistantReply
    #endregion
}
```

## Page template (minimal page)

```razor
@page "/your-route"

@inherits BaseComponent

<PageTitle>Your Page</PageTitle>

<!-- markup -->

@code {
    // [Parameter] properties
    // shared state
    // lifecycle overrides

    #region # <Grouped feature>
    #endregion

    #region # Helpers
    #endregion
}
```

Markup-only pages with no logic may use an empty `@code { }` or omit `@code` entirely.
